SEND: {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "--- FILE: /data/data/com.termux/files/home/Projects/ComputeRes/README.md (120 lines) ---\n   1 | <div align=\"center\">\n   2 |   <h1>\ud83c\udf0c ComputeRes</h1>\n   3 |   <p><strong>The Operating System Built Exclusively for Artificial Intelligence.</strong></p>\n   4 |   \n   5 |   [![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)\n   6 |   [![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)\n   7 |   [![Docker Ready](https://img.shields.io/badge/docker-ready-2496ED.svg?logo=docker)](https://www.docker.com/)\n   8 |   [![ZeroMQ IPC](https://img.shields.io/badge/IPC-ZeroMQ-DF0000.svg)](https://zeromq.org/)\n   9 |   [![WebRTC Mesh](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2P-WebRTC-333333.svg)](https://webrtc.org/)\n  10 |   [![Wasmtime Sandboxing](https://img.shields.io/badge/Security-WASM-654FF0.svg)](https://wasmtime.dev/)\n  11 | </div>\n  12 | \n  13 | ---\n  14 | \n  15 | ## \ud83d\ude80 The Philosophy\n  16 | **ComputeRes does not have a brain.** It does not contain an LLM. It does not think. \n  17 | \n  18 | It is the **Environment**. \n  19 | \n  20 | It is a mathematically rigorous, mathematically secure, decentralized operating system exposed entirely via the **Model Context Protocol (MCP)**. External AI agents connect to this OS to possess it, execute workloads, compile code, and orchestrate decentralized swarms across the globe.\n  21 | \n  22 | ---\n  23 | \n  24 | ## \ud83e\udde0 Core Architecture\n  25 | \n  26 | ComputeRes solves the three hardest problems in AI Agent deployment: **Inter-Process Communication (IPC)**, **Security Sandboxing**, and **Decentralized Swarming**.\n  27 | \n  28 | 1. **The Kernel (ZeroMQ):** An ultra-fast, non-blocking asynchronous `ROUTER/DEALER` broker that mathematically queues intents from external LLMs and routes them to internal OS workers instantly.\n  29 | 2. **The Sandbox (Wasmtime):** AI Agents are inherently untrustworthy. Every system operation is executed within a strict WebAssembly (WASM) container enforcing absolute memory capping and CPU instruction metering (\"Fuel\"). If an agent writes infinite loops, the OS cuts its fuel and kills it gracefully.\n  30 | 3. **The Swarm Mesh (WebRTC):** ComputeRes utilizes `aiortc` (SCTP over DTLS over UDP) to punch through NAT firewalls, allowing multiple ComputeRes nodes running on laptops, edge devices, and servers to sync decentralized state schemas via CRDTs without a centralized cloud.\n  31 | \n  32 | *For deep architectural blueprints, see the [Architecture Directory](plan/docker_aiortc_blueprint.md).*\n  33 | \n  34 | ---\n  35 | \n  36 | ## \u26a1 Deployment: The Zero-Compilation Matrix\n  37 | \n  38 | Deploying C-extensions (like WebRTC codecs and ZeroMQ bindings) usually destroys CI/CD pipelines. ComputeRes is engineered to deploy in **under 15 seconds**.\n  39 | \n  40 | By locking the architecture to `python:3.10-slim-bullseye`, we guarantee the resolution of pre-compiled `manylinux2014` wheels. \n  41 | \n  42 | ```bash\n  43 | # 1. Clone the Matrix\n  44 | git clone https://github.com/polymath-void/ComputeRes.git\n  45 | cd ComputeRes\n  46 | \n  47 | # 2. Build the OS (Takes < 15 seconds)\n  48 | docker build -t compute_res-core .\n  49 | \n  50 | # 3. Boot the Kernel (Host networking for WebRTC UDP performance)\n  51 | docker run -d --name compute_res-kernel --network host compute_res-core\n  52 | ```\n  53 | \n  54 | ---\n  55 | \n  56 | ## \ud83d\udcf1 Hardware Capabilities: Rooted vs. Non-Rooted Edge Devices\n  57 | \n  58 | ComputeRes is designed to run everywhere\u2014from AWS clusters down to Android smartphones in your pocket. \n  59 | \n  60 | ### \ud83d\udfe2 Rooted Devices & Standard OS (Linux, macOS, Windows)\n  61 | If you have root access to `cgroups` and namespaces (e.g., standard servers, laptops, or rooted Android devices), we **strongly recommend** the Docker deployment strategy above. The container isolates the WebRTC C-bindings and prevents capability bleeding from the Wasmtime engine.\n  62 | \n  63 | ### \ud83d\udfe1 Non-Rooted Environments (e.g., Android Termux)\n  64 | On heavily sandboxed, non-rooted edge devices, the Docker Daemon (`dockerd`) cannot run natively. However, the **ComputeRes Kernel is fully OS-agnostic**. \n  65 | \n  66 | You can bypass Docker entirely and boot the OS directly into the native Python runtime environment:\n  67 | \n  68 | ```bash\n  69 | # 1. Install directly from PyPI (Core OS only - bypasses WebRTC C-compilers)\n  70 | pip install compute_res\n  71 | \n  72 | # (Optional) If you want full WebRTC capability natively on Android Termux:\n  73 | # Run the included Termux build optimizer which natively compiles PyAV C-bindings\n  74 | # and bypasses the GNU libc.so.6 constraints:\n  75 | chmod +x termux_setup.sh\n  76 | ./termux_setup.sh\n  77 | \n  78 | # 2. Boot the native Kernel in one tab\n  79 | compute_res\n  80 | \n  81 | # 3. Boot the Telemetry TUI Dashboard in a second tab\n  82 | python3 -m compute_res.telemetry.core.app\n  83 | ```\n  84 | *Note: The native python deployment seamlessly maps the `~/.compute_res/tools/` filesystem in your home directory to maintain structural consistency without container volumes.*\n  85 | \n  86 | ---\n  87 | \n  88 | ## \ud83d\udd0c Connecting your AI (The MCP Protocol)\n  89 | \n  90 | ComputeRes natively exposes the **Model Context Protocol (FastMCP)** via standard input/output. This means you can plug ComputeRes into any AI client (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Gemini, or custom swarms) by adding it to your `mcp_config.json`:\n  91 | \n  92 | ```json\n  93 | {\n  94 |   \"mcpServers\": {\n  95 |     \"compute_res\": {\n  96 |       \"command\": \"python3\",\n  97 |       \"args\": [\"/absolute/path/to/ComputeRes/compute_res/gateway/mcp_server.py\"]\n  98 |     }\n  99 |   }\n 100 | }\n 101 | ```\n 102 | *Note: Make sure the `compute_res-kernel` daemon is running in the background to handle the ZeroMQ routing!*\n 103 | \n 104 | ---\n 105 | \n 106 | ## \ud83e\udd1d Calling All Engineers (Contribute!)\n 107 | \n 108 | ComputeRes is bleeding-edge. We are actively pushing the boundaries of what autonomous LLM swarms can do on bare-metal systems. \n 109 | \n 110 | **We need your help to build the future:**\n 111 | * **Rust/WASM Engineers:** Help us optimize the Wasmtime memory bounds and build tighter capability sandboxes.\n 112 | * **Network Architects:** We need stress tests on the WebRTC UDP hole-punching for massive swarm synchronization.\n 113 | * **Core Python Devs:** Optimize the `asyncio` loop handling the ZeroMQ `ROUTER/DEALER` broker.\n 114 | \n 115 | **To Contribute:**\n 116 | 1. Fork the repo.\n 117 | 2. Check out the [Architectural Blueprints](plan/).\n 118 | 3. Submit a PR. We review everything. \n 119 | \n 120 | Star the repo \u2b50 if you believe in the future of Agentic Operating Systems.\n"}]}}
